{
  "tema": 6081,
  "slug": "superlativo-isimo-cambios",
  "titulo": "Superlatives with -ísimo: adjectives ending in -co, -go, -ble, -z, -or and -n",
  "subtitulo": "Rico → riquísimo, largo → larguísimo, amable → amabilísimo.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "-ísimo with spelling changes: -co → -quísimo, -go → -guísimo, -ble → -bilísimo, -z → -císimo, and -or / -n add -císimo.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**-ísimo** (_extremely_) needs a spelling change with some endings, to keep the sound or because of tradition."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Ending",
            "Change",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "-co",
              "-co → -quísimo",
              "rico → riquísimo"
            ],
            [
              "-go",
              "-go → -guísimo",
              "largo → larguísimo"
            ],
            [
              "-ble",
              "-ble → -bilísimo",
              "amable → amabilísimo"
            ],
            [
              "-z",
              "-z → -císimo",
              "feliz → felicísimo, capaz → capacísimo"
            ],
            [
              "-or, -n",
              "add -císimo",
              "joven → jovencísimo, trabajador → trabajadorcísimo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "All of them agree in gender and number: **riquísima**, **larguísimos**, **amabilísimas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **-co** and **-go** changes keep the hard sound: **c** before **i** would sound like _s_, and **g** before **i** like an English _h_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: think of **riquísimo** tacos. If you can say that one, you can say them all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Estos tacos están ==riquísimos==.",
              "en": "These tacos are delicious."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi abuela tenía el pelo ==larguísimo==.",
              "en": "My grandma had super long hair."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tienen que ser ==amabilísimos== con ella.",
              "en": "They have to be extremely kind to her."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hoy estoy ==felicísimo==: ¡hubo olas!",
              "en": "I'm super happy today: there were waves!"
            },
            {
              "es": "Se ve ==jovencísima== para su edad.",
              "en": "She looks very young for her age."
            },
            {
              "es": "El café está ==fresquísimo==.",
              "en": "The coffee is super fresh."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
